# Lock-Free SPSC Ring Buffer in Rust

## Conceptual Overview

A Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) ring buffer is one of the simplest lock-free data structures. The key insight is that with exactly one producer and one consumer, we can manage the head (write) and tail (read) indices using atomic operations without locks or more complex multi-writer/multi-reader coordination.

The buffer consists of:
- A fixed-size array of slots
- An atomic write index (managed by producer)
- An atomic read index (managed by consumer)
- Slot state tracking (occupied vs. free) to handle the modulo-wrapping and ensure visibility

